{
  "window_id": "w0020",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "field": "date",
      "predicted": "2018-08-09",
      "symptom": "Month digit misread by OCR; receipt header line is '09/03/2018' but the pipeline committed the August interpretation. Diagnoser visual check of 034 shows date printed as '09/03/2018' in the header near 'Date:' / 'Time:'."
    },
    {
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "702.00",
      "symptom": "Receipt has several TOTAL-matching lines (Subtotal, Total Excl. of GST 96.23, Total Incl. of GST 102.00, Total Amt Rounded 102.00, Payment 102.00). OCR corrupted the final 'Total Amt Rounded' value to 702.00. Current lowest-tier selector takes the LAST candidate and so returns the corrupted value even though three other TOTAL/AMOUNT lines agree on 102.00."
    },
    {
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "23.26",
      "symptom": "Receipt has 'Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26', 'Rounding Adj: -0.01', and a final bold standalone 'TOTAL: 23.25'. Within priority tier 4, the earlier 'Total (Inclusive…)' line was returned instead of the final 'TOTAL:' line, so rounding adjustment was ignored."
    },
    {
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "\"\" (empty string)",
      "symptom": "Receipt clearly shows 'Grand Total : 92.80' (priority-1 keyword). Nothing was extracted, and the cell was written as an empty string rather than a real null/None. This is simultaneously an extraction miss and a schema-null-handling bug."
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "rc1_tier_selection_ambiguity",
      "area": "image-ocr: structured field extraction",
      "detail": "The guidance in image-ocr says to honor priority tiers and exclusions but is silent about which candidate to pick inside a tier when several lines match. Both 'first match' and 'last match' are wrong in different receipts: for 077 the LAST standalone 'TOTAL:' is the authoritative final value (post-rounding), while for 074 picking the LAST 'Total Amt Rounded' line surfaces an OCR-corrupted number instead of three consistent 102.00 lines. The skill lacks a tie-breaking rule that (a) prefers lines whose keyword is a standalone 'TOTAL' / 'GRAND TOTAL' / 'NET TOTAL' token at line start, and (b) cross-validates against other same-tier candidates when values disagree."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc2_rounded_total_precedence",
      "area": "image-ocr: priority tiering",
      "detail": "The task hint implies a single final value, but receipts frequently contain both a pre-rounding and a post-rounding total ('Total Rounded', 'Rounded Total (RM):', 'Total Amt Rounded', or a final bold 'TOTAL:' following a 'Rounding Adj' line). The current tiers do not promote the post-rounding/standalone final-TOTAL line above the earlier pre-rounding GST-inclusive subtotal, which caused 077 to miss the 0.01 adjustment."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc3_no_null_safe_schema_writer",
      "area": "xlsx: strict-schema outputs",
      "detail": "When extract_total returns None (as happened for 078), the pipeline wrote an empty string into the Excel cell instead of a real null. The xlsx skill documents the 'real null vs \"\" / \"nan\"' pitfall only in the candidate draft and only in prose; it does not give an actionable 'build row dict, then astype(object), then let pandas write real empty cells' recipe that an agent will reliably follow. It also does not warn that f-strings, ternaries and pandas default NaN conversion all silently produce string nulls."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc4_single_pass_ocr_for_dates",
      "area": "image-ocr: preprocessing / multi-pass",
      "detail": "Date digits on printed receipts are the single most OCR-fragile tokens (3 vs 8, 0 vs 6, 1 vs 7). The skill shows a multi_pass_ocr pattern for text coverage but does not apply it to date extraction specifically, nor does it combine outputs by voting. 034's '09/03/2018' was misread once as '09/08/2018' and that single hypothesis was committed."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc5_amount_regex_and_normalization_gaps",
      "area": "image-ocr: numeric parsing",
      "detail": "The current NUM_RE accepts thousand-separator and decimal forms but not (a) a bare integer followed by missing decimal (e.g. OCR'd '1000' for '10.00') or (b) comma-as-decimal European style ('20,00'). This is directly implicated in historical '052.jpg GRAND TOTAL 1000' handling and makes the skill brittle on noisy receipts even when the keyword line is correctly identified."
    }
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Structured-extraction section defines priority tiers and exclusions but no deterministic intra-tier tie-breaker; no explicit 'prefer standalone TOTAL / rounded-total line that appears AFTER a Rounding Adjustment line' rule."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Date extraction uses first regex match from a single OCR pass; no multi-pass consensus or digit-level sanity check, so a single misread digit silently commits."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Numeric parser does not degrade gracefully when OCR drops the decimal point ('1000' for '10.00') or substitutes a comma ('20,00'); no cross-candidate consistency check when the chosen total disagrees with Subtotal / Cash-Change arithmetic on the same receipt."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "process_receipt / per-image pipeline is described as 'returns None on failure' but the skill does not insist that callers write that None through to the final output without intermediate string coercion."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "Strict-schema section describes the 'real null vs empty string' pitfall but gives no single tight code recipe binding extractor outputs (Optional[str]) to Excel cells; agents end up writing '' or 'None' when a field is missing (observed in 078.jpg)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "No post-write verifier snippet that asserts, for each required column, that every cell is either None (empty) or a str matching the field's exact format (e.g. 'YYYY-MM-DD' or 'N.NN'); such a self-check would have caught the 078 empty-string case before submission."
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "In the Structured Field Extraction section, add an explicit intra-tier selection rule: within a tier, enumerate ALL non-excluded matches, then pick the candidate using this order: (1) a line whose keyword is a standalone token at line start (e.g. '^\\s*TOTAL\\b', '^\\s*GRAND\\s+TOTAL\\b', '^\\s*NETT?\\s+TOTAL\\b') that appears AFTER any 'ROUNDING ADJ' / 'ROUND(ED)?' line in the text, (2) otherwise the line with a '^\\s*TOTAL\\b' standalone token, (3) otherwise the LAST non-excluded match. Document that this implements the 'final total after rounding' convention common on Malaysian receipts."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a cross-candidate consistency check: after choosing a tier winner, if the selected numeric value disagrees with the MAJORITY value among the other non-excluded same-tier candidates by more than a cent, and the majority value is present in >= 2 other lines, prefer the majority value. This rescues 074-style single-line OCR corruptions while leaving well-formed receipts unchanged."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Promote 'ROUNDED TOTAL', 'TOTAL ROUNDED', 'TOTAL AMT ROUNDED', 'ROUNDED TOTAL (RM)' and standalone final 'TOTAL:' / 'TOTAL RM:' patterns into a new tier that sits ABOVE the generic 'TOTAL / AMOUNT' tier, so the post-rounding final value wins over earlier GST-inclusive subtotals. Keep 'GRAND TOTAL' and 'TOTAL (:) RM' at their current top positions."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "In Date Extraction, replace the single-pass single-match pattern with a multi-hypothesis strategy: run date regex over text produced by at least 2 preprocessing variants (grayscale+autocontrast, inverted, upscale 2x) and at least 2 PSM modes (6 and 11); collect candidates, canonicalize each to ISO; if multiple distinct ISO candidates exist, prefer the one appearing in the greatest number of passes (majority vote), breaking ties by earliest reading-order position. Return None when no pass yields a valid date."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Widen numeric handling: (a) allow a dot-missing fallback where a keyword-line integer is interpreted as 'X.XX' only when its length is >= 3 AND the surrounding tier's other candidates agree on that magnitude; (b) accept 'NN,NN' as decimal when no three-digit thousand group follows; (c) always strip leading currency tokens ('RM', '$', 'MYR') before conversion; (d) format outputs as f\"{v:.2f}\" strings. Document each branch with a one-line example."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Expand EXCLUSIONS with task-observed noise lines that leaked into totals in prior runs: 'TOTAL ITEMS', 'TOTAL QTY', 'TOTAL QUANTITY', 'TOTAL SAVINGS', 'ITEM COUNT', 'AVERAGE / PAX', 'AMOUNT(RM) TAX', and section headers 'GST SUMMARY' / 'TAX SUMMARY' (and ignore all lines after such a header when extracting totals)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "In Per-Image Pipeline, state as a hard contract: process_receipt MUST return a dict whose values are either a correctly-formatted str (date 'YYYY-MM-DD' or amount 'N.NN') or Python None — never '', 'None', 'nan', 0, or a float. Any downstream writer must propagate None untouched."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "In Strict-Schema Outputs, replace the current prose checklist with a copy-pasteable end-to-end recipe: build list-of-dicts with None for missing fields, construct DataFrame with explicit columns, df = df.astype({col: 'object' for col in required_cols}), df.sort_values('filename', kind='stable'), then pd.ExcelWriter(..., engine='openpyxl') to_excel(sheet_name='<exact>', index=False, na_rep=''). Explicitly warn: do NOT use df.fillna(''), do NOT use f-strings to coerce None, do NOT rely on pandas' default NaN -> blank behaviour (it works, but only if dtype stays object)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add a mandatory post-write verifier template: re-open the written file with openpyxl (data_only=True), assert sheet names == required, header row == required columns, every data row's missing fields are Python None (cell.value is None), every present amount matches r'^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$', every present date matches r'^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$', and rows are sorted ascending by filename. Fail loudly if any assertion breaks before the task is considered finished."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add a short 'Null vs Empty String: Observed Failure Mode' note citing the generic pattern (OCR pipeline returns None, agent writes '' via an f-string or a ternary that coerces None to ''), with a one-line fix pattern: `value = fields['total_amount'] if fields['total_amount'] is not None else None` — never `str(fields['total_amount'] or '')`."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": {
    "overall": 0.78,
    "notes": "Four failing cells are directly inspectable in the supplied receipt images and cleanly map to either a tier-selection rule (074, 077), a date-OCR single-pass weakness (034), or a null-handling bug in the Excel writer (078). Recommendations stay within the five existing SKILL.md files and generalize beyond these 22 receipts (post-rounding final-TOTAL precedence, multi-pass date voting, strict null propagation). Residual uncertainty concerns (a) whether the cross-candidate majority rule could occasionally override a correctly OCR'd final-rounded total that legitimately differs by rounding from pre-rounding candidates — mitigated by requiring >= 2 agreeing other lines and a > 0.01 gap; and (b) whether the oracle for 077 truly expects the post-rounding 23.25 — which the receipt image strongly supports but cannot be verified from permitted feedback alone."
  }
}
